---
import Card from "astro-theme-university/components/Card.astro";
import CardGrid from "astro-theme-university/components/CardGrid.astro";
import ContentLayout from "astro-theme-university/layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import { courseMeta } from "../course-config";
import { sessionLabels, siteConfig } from "../site-config";
---

<ContentLayout
  title={`${courseMeta.code}: ${courseMeta.title}`}
  description={courseMeta.description}
  {...siteConfig}
>
  <ul class="course-tags" aria-label="Course tags">
    {courseMeta.tags.map((tag) => <li>{tag}</li>)}
  </ul>

  <p class="core-question">
    Every week of this course argues toward one question: <strong>When does a coincidence become
    meaningful?</strong>
  </p>

  <section class="opening-moment">
    <p class="moment-text" data-moment>
      You're reading this the moment you opened it — which is the only fact this page can actually
      confirm.
    </p>
    <p class="moment-caption">
      Everything after that — what it means that you're here, today, reading this — is the rest of
      the course.
    </p>
  </section>

  <h2>What you will do</h2>
  <p>
    Every week you bring a real pattern to class — a dream, a headline, a losing streak, a
    recommendation algorithm that seemed to read your mind — and take it apart in public. You keep
    a running diary of coincidences you notice in your own life, build a small working "oracle" of
    your own design, and finish by writing the most honest possible account of one moment that felt
    like fate: what actually happened, what you told yourself happened, and how you'd tell the
    difference next time.
  </p>

  <h2>Who it is for</h2>
  <p>
    Anyone who has ever thought <em>that's too weird to be a coincidence</em> and wanted to know if
    they were right. No background in statistics, psychology or the occult is assumed — just a
    willingness to interrogate your own best stories about yourself. Comfort with first-year-level
    argument and evidence is the only prerequisite.
  </p>

  <h2>How the course thinks</h2>
  <ol class="philosophy">
    <li>
      <strong>Seeing patterns.</strong> Why brains that evolved to spot predators in leaves now see
      faces in toast, streaks in coin flips, and messages in static — and why that machinery
      basically never turns off.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Giving patterns meaning.</strong> How the same noticed pattern becomes a private
      superstition, a shared religion, a diagnosis, or a punchline — depending entirely on who is
      doing the interpreting, and what they needed it to mean.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Deciding what to trust.</strong> A working method for the moment a pattern shows up in
      your own life: what would make it worth acting on, and what would just make it worth noticing.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Where to go next</h2>
  <CardGrid columns={2}>
    <Card title={sessionLabels.plural} href="/sessions/">
      <p>The weekly schedule and what happens in each teaching session.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="Assessment" href="/assessments/">
      <p>What is marked, what it is worth, and when it is due.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="People" href="/people/">
      <p>Who teaches the course and how to reach them.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="Approach" href="/approach/">
      <p>Why the course is built this way, and what it deliberately avoids.</p>
    </Card>
  </CardGrid>

  <script>
    const el = document.querySelector<HTMLParagraphElement>("[data-moment]");
    if (el) {
      const now = new Date();
      const time = now.toLocaleTimeString(undefined, { hour: "numeric", minute: "2-digit" });
      const day = now.toLocaleDateString(undefined, { weekday: "long" });

      let visits = 1;
      try {
        const key = "slop3855:visits";
        visits = Number(localStorage.getItem(key) ?? "0") + 1;
        localStorage.setItem(key, String(visits));
      } catch {
        // Storage can be unavailable (private browsing, disabled cookies); the
        // sentence still works if it just calls this visit number one.
      }

      const visitClause =
        visits <= 1
          ? "the first time this browser has opened it"
          : `visit number ${visits} from this browser`;

      el.textContent = `You opened this page at ${time} on a ${day} — ${visitClause}.`;
    }
  </script>
</ContentLayout>

<style>
  .course-tags {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-block: 0 2rem;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .course-tags li {
    padding: 0.25rem 0.65rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: var(--at-text-secondary);
    background: var(--at-bg-alt);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .core-question {
    font-size: var(--at-font-size-h3);
    line-height: var(--at-line-height-heading);
    margin-block-end: 2rem;
  }

  .opening-moment {
    padding: var(--at-spacing-lg);
    border: 1px solid var(--at-border);
    border-radius: var(--at-border-radius);
    background: var(--at-bg-alt);
    margin-block-end: 2rem;
  }

  .moment-text {
    font-size: var(--at-font-size-h4);
    margin-block-end: 0.5rem;
  }

  .moment-caption {
    color: var(--at-text-secondary);
    font-size: var(--at-font-size-sm);
    margin-block-end: 0;
  }

  .philosophy {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding-inline-start: 1.25rem;
  }

  .philosophy li::marker {
    color: var(--at-heading);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
